.TH "shellkin\-feature" "5" "March 2026" "shellkin\-feature(5)" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]shellkin\-feature\f[R] \- feature file for shellkin
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shellkin feature files use a small Gherkin\-compatible subset for
describing test scenarios.
.PP
Feature files are loaded from the selected features directory and must
use the \f[B].feature\f[R] extension.
.SH SUPPORTED KEYWORDS
Shellkin currently supports these Gherkin keywords:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Feature\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Background\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Scenario\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Given\f[R], \f[B]When\f[R], \f[B]Then\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], \f[B]*\f[R]
.SH FORMAT
.SS Feature Header
Each feature file starts with a \f[B]Feature:\f[R] header.
.IP
.EX
Feature: \-\-help
.EE
.SS Description Text
Free text may appear below the feature header before the first section.
.IP
.EX
Feature: \-\-help
  Show help message
.EE
.SS Scenario
Each executable example is declared with \f[B]Scenario:\f[R].
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Run \-\-help
  When I run \(aqshellkin \-\-help\(aq
  Then the output should include \(aqshellkin COMMAND\(aq
.EE
.SS Background
Use \f[B]Background:\f[R] for steps that should run before each scenario
in the feature.
.IP
.EX
Background:
  Given I am in a temp directory
.EE
.SS Steps
Supported step keywords are \f[B]Given\f[R], \f[B]When\f[R],
\f[B]Then\f[R], \f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], and \f[B]*\f[R].
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Touch a file
  Given I am in a temp directory
  When I run \(aqtouch somefile\(aq
  Then the file \(aqsomefile\(aq should exist
.EE
.PP
\f[B]And\f[R], \f[B]But\f[R], and \f[B]*\f[R] reuse the semantic type of
the previous step.
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Run command
  When I run \(aqshellkin \-\-help\(aq
  And the exit code should mean success
.EE
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Prepare files
  Given I am in a temp directory
  When I run \(aqtouch one\(aq
  * I run \(aqtouch two\(aq
  Then the file \(aqone\(aq should exist
  And the file \(aqtwo\(aq should exist
.EE
.PP
Like \f[B]And\f[R] and \f[B]But\f[R], the \f[B]*\f[R] keyword cannot be
the first step in a scenario or background.
.SH COMMENTS AND BLANK LINES
Blank lines are ignored.
.PP
Lines starting with \f[B]#\f[R] are treated as comments.
.IP
.EX
# This is a comment
Feature: Example
.EE
.SH DOC STRINGS
Shellkin supports Gherkin\-style doc strings using
\f[B]\(dq\(dq\(dq\f[R] fences.
.IP
.EX
Scenario: Match multiline output
  When I run \(aqprintf \(dqhello\(rsnworld\(dq\(aq
  Then the output should match
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    hello
    world
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
.EE
.PP
The doc string content is exposed to the matching step definition
through the \f[B]DOC_STRING\f[R] environment variable.
.SH UNSUPPORTED CONSTRUCTS
The following common Gherkin constructs are not currently supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Rule\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Scenario Outline\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Examples\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
data tables
.IP \(bu 2
tags such as \f[B]\(atslow\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
Feature: file creation
  Basic file operations

Background:
  Given I am in a temp directory

Scenario: Create a file
  When I run \(aqtouch somefile\(aq
  Then the file \(aqsomefile\(aq should exist
.EE
